{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1205417","title":"Enhancing Concurrent Production of Volatile Fatty Acids and Phosphorus Minerals from Waste Activated Sludge via Magnesium Ferrate Pre-Oxidation","description":"This study investigated the strategy of magnesium ferrate (MF) pre-oxidation to enhance acidogenic fermentation of waste activated sludge (WAS), targeting the simultaneous production of volatile fatty acids (VFAs) and phosphorus-minerals (struvite and vivianite). Investigation reveals that the MF pre-oxidation raised the pH, enhanced key hydrolases activity, enriched acidogens and iron-reducing bacteria for driving the concurrent production of VFAs and phosphorus-minerals (struvite and vivianite). A schematic illustration was proposed to reveal the underlying mechanisms related to biotransformation enhancement of VFAs and formations of struvite and vivianite via WAS acidogenic fermentation by MF pre-oxidation. This study provided an effective strategy for realizing concurrent production of high-purity VFAs along with struvite and vivianite from WAS.","center":"Dongguan University of Technology","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2025/01/01 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN46049089","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2024-05-10",2024,"CN","Guangdong",1812545,"Dongguan","probable",null,null,"China:Dongguan",null,null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN46049090","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2024-05-10",2024,"CN","Guangdong",1812545,"Dongguan","probable",null,null,"China:Dongguan",null,null,null,null,"city-level location without 